/**
	Returns the current time as a Unix timestamp, that is the number of whole seconds that have passed since midnight UTC on January 1st, 1970.
	const uint64 TIME_STAMP;
	## Remarks:
		The value comes from the system clock, so it changes if the user changes their system time. To measure how much time has passed while your program runs, use a `timer` or the `ticks()` function instead.
		Unix timestamps are a convenient way to save a point in time to a file, for example to remember when a player last played. For more detailed date and time handling, see the `datetime` and `timestamp` classes.
*/

// Example:
void main() {
	alert("Example", TIME_STAMP + " seconds have passed since January 1st, 1970.");
}
